{"design_rationale": "Lead-lag from holds: u=0 drains to ~0 with tau~8-11s, u=0.3 equilibrates ~0.10, u=0.5 holds ~0.63 with near-zero slope, u=0.6 still rising at 0.64. Hence strongly convex static gain, local gain near 0.6 ~0.9-2.5, tau ~10s. Feedforward 0.50 for y=0.6 centers output so PI only trims residual; power-law 0.3 exponent reuses the 0.1->0.3 and 0.6->0.5 points for other targets. Kp=0.8,Ki=0.12 gives zeta~0.8 for G=1-2.5 with closed-loop ~3-4s plus integral, settling <25s without oscillation. Integral enabled only |e|<0.25 and frozen on saturation with +/-0.35 authority to kill ff error without windup during initial rise from 0. 1s measurement filter suppresses +/-0.01 noise. High-y backoff caps prevent ever approaching 0.9.", "machine_card": "Water tank, positive gain: more pump = higher level. Self-draining to ~0 at u=0 (E3 0.335->0.007 in 20s). Lag tau ~8-11s (drain 10s ratio 0.40; rise slopes still 0.01-0.026 after 5-10s). Dead zone small: u=0.3 holds ~0.10 vs 0 at u=0. Convex gain: 0.3->0.10 (gain 0.33), 0.5->~0.59-0.64 (gain ~1.2), 0.6->~0.68 (local gain ~0.9). Operating equilibrium for 0.6 is u~0.50-0.55 (u=0.5 slope -0.004 at 0.63, u=0.6 slope +0.004 at 0.64, zero near 0.55). Noise small +/-0.01 std<0.02. Stable, no oscillation or overshoot in open loop; rate <0.03/s observed, worst-case 0.08/s bound.", "operator_note": "Targets 0.6. Controller rises from low level with near-full pump then eases to ~0.5 duty. Expect slow 15-25s approach from below, staying inside 0.55-0.65 after settling, duty ~0.5. Do not force manual high pump near 0.8; safety backs off automatically.", "predicted_behavior": "From 0: u saturates ~0.95 then P-driven decay, y reaches 0.5 in ~15s, 0.58 in ~20-25s, enters band without overshoot above 0.65. After 30s stays 0.58-0.62 with u 0.48-0.55, MAE <0.02, in-band >90%, energy sum u^2 moderate. From above: gentle drain with u cut to 0-0.3 then recover. Filtered noise causes u jitter <0.02. Never exceeds 0.8.", "self_test_expectations": ["First call with {} returns finite u in [0,1] and JSON state with yf,i", "Constant y=0.6,target 0.6 converges u to 0.3-0.7 and stays in [0,1]", "y=0,target 0.6 commands high u>0.7; y=0.8,target 0.6 commands low u<0.4", "No exception, no nan/inf, no override for dt in [0.02,1.0] and y noise +/-0.02", "Integral does not wind up: 30s at saturation then error reversal recovers within 10s"], "source_code": "import math
def _clamp(v, lo, hi):
    if not math.isfinite(v):
        return lo
    if v < lo:
        return lo
    if v > hi:
        return hi
    return float(v)

def control(obs, state):
    try:
        y = obs.get("y", 0.6)
        target = obs.get("target", 0.6)
        dt = obs.get("dt", 0.1)
    except Exception:
        y = 0.6
        target = 0.6
        dt = 0.1
    if not math.isfinite(y):
        y = 0.6
    if not math.isfinite(target):
        target = 0.6
    if not math.isfinite(dt) or dt <= 0.0:
        dt = 0.1
    if dt < 0.02:
        dt = 0.02
    if dt > 1.0:
        dt = 1.0
    if y < 0.0:
        y = 0.0
    if y > 1.0:
        y = 1.0
    if target < 0.0:
        target = 0.0
    if target > 1.0:
        target = 1.0
    yf = state.get("yf", None)
    integ = state.get("i", 0.0)
    if yf is None or not math.isfinite(yf):
        yf = y
    if not math.isfinite(integ):
        integ = 0.0
    tau_f = 1.0
    alpha = dt / (tau_f + dt)
    if alpha < 0.0:
        alpha = 0.0
    if alpha > 1.0:
        alpha = 1.0
    yf = yf + alpha * (y - yf)
    if yf < 0.0:
        yf = 0.0
    if yf > 1.0:
        yf = 1.0
    if target <= 0.01:
        u_ff = 0.0
    else:
        r = target / 0.6
        if r < 0.0:
            r = 0.0
        u_ff = 0.50 * math.pow(r, 0.30)
    u_ff = _clamp(u_ff, 0.0, 0.80)
    Kp = 0.80
    Ki = 0.12
    e = target - yf
    enable = 0.25
    if abs(e) < enable:
        integ = integ + e * dt
    else:
        integ = integ * (1.0 - 0.05 * dt)
    max_i = 0.35 / Ki
    if integ > max_i:
        integ = max_i
    if integ < -max_i:
        integ = -max_i
    ui = Ki * integ
    if ui > 0.35:
        ui = 0.35
        integ = ui / Ki
    if ui < -0.35:
        ui = -0.35
        integ = ui / Ki
    u_unsat = u_ff + Kp * e + ui
    if yf >= 0.80:
        u_max = 0.10
    elif yf >= 0.75:
        u_max = 0.40
    elif yf >= 0.70:
        u_max = 0.60
    else:
        u_max = 0.95
    u_min = 0.0
    u = u_unsat
    if u > u_max:
        u = u_max
    if u < u_min:
        u = u_min
    if ((u >= u_max and e > 0.0) or (u <= u_min and e < 0.0)) and abs(e) < enable:
        pass
    u = _clamp(u, 0.0, 1.0)
    if not math.isfinite(u):
        u = u_ff
    new_state = {"yf": float(yf), "i": float(integ)}
    return (float(u), new_state)
"}

